  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1242 PM MDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nThe upper ridge will amplify over the region on Friday and Saturday, \nwith the center of the high pressure settling just south of \nColorado. This will give us a brief period of warmer and slightly \ndrier conditions. High temperatures will be in the mid-high 90s out \neast, with some portions of the eastern plains exceeding 100 degrees \non Saturday. The monsoon plume will be moved out of our immediate \narea, but lingering moisture at the mid to low-levels, combined with \ndiurnal heating, will still allow for isolated to scattered \nconvection each afternoon over the mountains.\n\nOn Sunday, the ridge will shift east as an upper low moves onshore \nfrom the Pacific Northwest, bringing a new surge of moisture into \nour area. Daily showers/storms will increase in strength and \ncoverage over the mountains, with more storms moving over the \neastern plains as well. Cooler air will move in behind a cold front \nsometime on Monday, with temperatures settling back around seasonal \nnormals.",
